{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1127453-triumph-casque-of-sorrows","id":1127453,"title":"Triumph Casque of Sorrows","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-10T19:45:24-07:00","id":1127453,"title":"Triumph Casque of Sorrows","content":"I know that the Triumph Casque of Sorrows is the ultimate doomsday device in the C:tD setting. But I can't recall if it's ever really stated exactly what it does. Anyone have a reference on this? If not, what do you think it does?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T21:38:45-07:00","id":1127914,"title":"","content":"It was never detailed.<br /> Maybe it would have gotten some further description in Keys to the Kingdom, but...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T19:08:04-07:00","id":1128297,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's what I thought. Okay, so let's speculate.....what the heck does it do? Why is it such an impressive doomsday device?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T07:59:15-07:00","id":1128821,"title":"","content":"i always imagined it was a helmet that rallied/awoke the formorian horde while also possessing the wearer and turning them into some sort of unholy/evil formorian overlorde","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T11:05:52-07:00","id":1128877,"title":"","content":"There are multiple references on what it does or what it might do. My recollection is that it is powerful of causing widespread destruction involving poison and fire even when unopened, and that opening the casque results in destroying anything (with no defense to it!) it is opened against. It's also not clear if the casque is actually something that must be stored in one's heart based on the Red King's use of it.<br /> <br /> Here are some references specifically to the Triumph Casque:<br /> <br /> From Dreams and Nightmares, Page 77 (copyright 1997):<br /> <br /> &quot;Encased in lead since the earliest times, this legendary treasure has never been used in the memory of any living creature, chimera or fae. According to the White Fomorians, the Triumph Casque is a 'weapon against which defense is impossible,' enabling whoever possesses it to eradicate anyone and anything without fear of reprisal or failure. It is believed that the Casque operates through principles common to both fire and poison, eradicating whatever it is opened to destroy in a singularly painful fashion.&quot;<br /> <br /> From Denizens of the Dreaming, Page 21 (copyright 1999):<br /> <br /> &quot;At the center of the conflict [the Tessarakonta, aka the War of Trees, specifically on the plane of Kureksarra in the Near Dreaming], the Red King of the fomorians wielded the Triumph Casque of Sorrows, a weapon of unspeakable power. Even unopened, its effects were devastating, raining poison and fire down upon his enemies as they sought to stand against him.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Pursuant to oaths made and broken, the Lords of the Mound attempted to wrest the casque from the Red King's heart, slaying an entire army of their former allies in the process. Betrayal wrought betrayal, and the Dreaming and Fate punished the Lords of the Mound's valiant efforts . . . . [Descriptions of various ways the Lords of the Mound were killed off, including possible alternative suggestions].&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;This action seemed to destroy the will of the fomorian hosts. Perhaps the Lords partially succeeded, making it too costly for the Red King to open the casque and destroy his enemies; perhaps the Red King foresaw that indirect conflict would ultimately be more successful. It matters little. What does matter is that he shattered the casque's key and cast the parts into his enemies' camps where they would sow eternal strife, before plucking the casque from his heart and dying. [His army had to flee, remaining fomorians were trapped by the Tuatha who imprisoned the White Court and the Red Court, while the Green Court voluntarily exiled themselves, then the Silver Ban is made permanent by the Tuatha].&quot;<br /> <br /> From Denizens of the Dreaming, Page 93 (copyright 1999):<br /> <br /> &quot;A weapon of unspeakable power, even unopened its effects were immense, raining poison and fire down upon its bearer's enemies as they sought to stand against him. Rumors of its power when opened speak of the utter annihilation of its foes, instantaneously rendering them nothing more than ash. it is said that there are no defenses against the casque's powers. Though the Red Fomorian king broke the casque's key into nine fragments, rumor tells that some have been reassembled, and with each other, another calamity threatens. Two key fragments have been assembled; two fomorian courts now awaken . . . .&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","user":"Imperator","date":". 08-14-2017, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T17:31:18-07:00","id":1131957,"title":"","content":"The poison and fire of the Casque of sorrows sound so similar, at least poetically, to a Nuclear bomb. Fire and Poison falling from the sky. Ash and Radiation. The allusion is reinforced with the casque being made of lead. I wonder who or what dreamed the casque? <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}